---
title: "Backgrounds"
description: "Background color, alpha, gradients, and clipping."
section: Utilities
sectionOrder: 3
order: 6
---

`--bg` is the color; `--bg-alpha` multiplies into its alpha without touching the text. A gradient pairs a type with its stops: `--bg-linear: to bottom in oklch; --bg-stops: var(--color-shade-600), transparent 20%`. `--bg: none` clears the color and any gradient, at the base or a state.

`--bg-clip` sets `background-clip`: `border-box`, `padding-box`, `content-box`, or `text`. With `text` the background shows only through the glyphs, so gradient text is `--bg-linear: to right; --bg-stops: var(--color-primary), var(--color-info-foreground); --bg-clip: text; --text: transparent`. It takes no tiers or states.

